# Which country has the most time zones?
subtitle: "Russia? The USA? Guess which country runs the most clocks, then hear why the answer is France, and why vast China gets by with just one."

## Which country has the most time zones?
affirm: playful
text: {"font_size":34}
use: bar_chart
with:
    labels:
      - ''
      - ''
      - ''
      - ''
    values:
      - 11
      - 11
      - 12
      - 1
    value_labels: false
    ylim:
      - 0
      - 16
    y_label: Time zones
    box:
      x: 130
      'y': 280
      w: 740
      h: 350
sources:
    - id: tad
      title: Which country has the most time zones?
      authors: timeanddate.com
      year: 2025
      url: https://www.timeanddate.com/time/country-with-the-most-time-zones.html
      finding: France uses 12 time zones (13 with its Antarctic claim), Russia and the USA 11 each; China uses one

    icon island at.data [2.55,14.7] cites ["tad"] size 90 set twemoji icon_look picture of "desert island" hidden true
    text overseas "islands!" #b5482e at.data [3.2,14.7] font_size 44 hidden true
    text beijing "Beijing time" #2f6b8f at.data [3,5.6] font_size 36 hidden true
    icon sunrise at.data [3,8.6] size 90 set twemoji icon_look picture of sunrise hidden true
    text daytime "always day somewhere" #b5482e at.data [3.05,11] font_size 30 hidden true
    text v1 "11" #3d3833 at.data [0,12.2] font_size 44 hidden true
    text v2 "11" #3d3833 at.data [1,12.2] font_size 44 hidden true
    text v3 "12" #3d3833 at.data [2,13.2] font_size 44 hidden true
    text v4 "1" #3d3833 at.data [3,2.2] font_size 44 hidden true
    path main1 #b5482e points [[1.72,0.5],[2.28,0.5]] data true style.stroke_width 10 hidden true
    text main1_l "1 mainland" #b5482e at.data [2,2.2] font_size 28 hidden true
    icon fl1 at.data [0,-1.6] size 56 set twemoji icon_look picture of "flag russia" hidden true
    text cn1 "Russia" at.data [0,-3.6] font_size 30 hidden true
    icon fl2 at.data [1,-1.6] size 56 set twemoji icon_look picture of "flag united states" hidden true
    text cn2 "USA" at.data [1,-3.6] font_size 30 hidden true
    icon fl3 at.data [2,-1.6] size 56 set twemoji icon_look picture of "flag france" hidden true
    text cn3 "France" at.data [2,-3.6] font_size 30 hidden true
    icon fl4 at.data [3,-1.6] size 56 set twemoji icon_look picture of "flag china" hidden true
    text cn4 "China" at.data [3,-3.6] font_size 30 hidden true
    text sun10 "sunrise after 10 am" #b5482e at.data [3.15,11.4] font_size 30 hidden true

    card title "Which country has the most time zones?"

A: Which country on Earth has the most time zones?
    draw axes fl1 fl2 fl3 fl4 cn1 cn2 cn3 cn4 parallel true

B: Easy. Russia. It's the biggest country there is.

    quiz "Which country has the most time zones?" on_canvas true
        right: France, with twelve, thanks to islands and territories scattered around the globe.
        wrong: Think of islands, not land.
        * Russia
        * United States
        + France
        * China

A: Russia has eleven. The United States, counting its Pacific islands, also has eleven.
    draw bar_1 v1 bar_2 v2 parallel true

B: France? Mainland France would fit inside Texas!
    draw bar_3 v3

The mainland has just one clock.
    draw main1 main1_l

A: But Tahiti, Guadeloupe, Réunion and New Caledonia are France too, each on its own time.
    draw island overseas

B: And China? It's almost as wide as the United States.
    draw bar_4 v4

A: One time zone. All of China runs on Beijing time.
    draw beijing

A: So in the far west, a winter sunrise comes after ten in the morning.
    draw sunrise sun10

    erase sunrise beijing sun10

B: So the sun never sets on France?
    highlight bar_3

A: Just about. From Polynesia to the  (@draw daytime@)Indian Ocean, it is nearly always daytime somewhere in France.

